fact WorkItem(id: "WI-144", description: some(value: "Proposal 032 — drop legacy 'conclusion' KB field after smt-gen migration. Once WI-143 lands, the kb/mod.rs RuleEntry.conclusion: Vec<TermId> field, the rule_conclusion(rid) accessor, and the assert_rule_debruijn_with_conclusion helper are all dead code. Cleanup: (a) remove the conclusion field from RuleEntry; (b) remove rule_conclusion getter; (c) collapse assert_rule_debruijn_with_conclusion back into assert_rule_debruijn; (d) simplify the loader's load_rule (kb/load.rs ~line 3918) to call assert_rule_debruijn directly without manufacturing an empty conclusion. Also reconsider the loader's transitional translation: now that smt-gen consumes head-as-conclusion natively, labeled non-equational rules can use the user's head directly as the KB head (no synthesized 0-arg label functor), provided the citation gate is rewritten to look up by label rather than head functor. That citation gate refactor is a sibling work item — see comments in load.rs load_rule for context. Acceptance: cargo test green; the conclusion field has zero references in the workspace."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-143", "WI-145"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-16T19:29:28Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-144", author: "user", content: "Blocked by WI-145 (the labeled-multi-head case is the only consumer of conclusion-vec; WI-145 is scoped to make labeled multi-head work end-to-end via label-citation, which is what frees the conclusion field). Unclaimed; will re-attempt WI-144 as the trivial cleanup after WI-145 lands.", at: "2026-05-16T16:58:32Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-144", author: "user", content: "Mechanical deletion after WI-145 freed the conclusion path. Dropped from rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/mod.rs: (a) RuleEntry.conclusion field; (b) rule_conclusion(rid) accessor; (c) assert_rule_debruijn_with_conclusion helper (inlined back into assert_rule_debruijn); (d) the conclusion parameter from finalize_rule_debruijn; the in_frame caller now matches the simpler signature. simplify pass: tried removing the #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)] on finalize_rule_debruijn since the dropped param took the count from 9 to 8, but clippy counts &mut self in its 7-arg limit so the allow is still needed at 8. Tests: full workspace cargo test --no-fail-fast green (45/45 binaries, 0 failures); lf1 discharge.sh 14 proved / 0 failed. Zero remaining conclusion-API references in the workspace (one accurate spec mention left in set_rule_label's doc comment about head-as-conclusion encoding — that's prose, not a stale reference).", at: "2026-05-16T19:29:28Z")
